[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3 uid="uid://shelfunit0sfgdmvp"]

; SHELF-1 (2026-09-19) — ONE BAY OF SUPERMARKET SHELVING. Four of these end to end make one
; aisle in SearchRoom.tscn; the end-cap that closes an aisle is EndCap.tscn, the same
; construction 0.9 m shorter.
;
; 2.30 m long (x) x 1.80 m tall (y) x 0.50 m deep (z), origin at the FLOOR, centred on the bay.
; Two uprights and three shelf boards, every one a BoxShape3D with a matching BoxMesh — the
; packet's construction verbatim. No back panel, deliberately: a bay you can see and shove a can
; THROUGH is what makes an aisle a place you root around in rather than a wall with tins on it,
; and it is what lets a product knocked off one side land on the floor of the other.
;
; SHELF HEIGHTS 0.40 / 0.95 / 1.50 (board centres; boards are 0.05 thick, so the standing
; surfaces are 0.425 / 0.975 / 1.525). The gaps are 0.50 m clear, which is the number the tallest
; product has to live inside: a cereal box is 0.28 m tall and rides at 0.14 above the board.
; 1.80 m is eye height plus a little, so the top of a bay HIDES the aisle behind it from a
; standing player — the whole reason the room is worth searching.
;
; ONE GREY, AND IT IS NOT THE WALLS'. SearchRoom's walls are a cool green-grey (0.43, 0.50, 0.44);
; this is a light neutral grey a clear step lighter and off the green axis, so four aisles read as
; four aisles in a capture instead of dissolving into the room. Flat, unshaded-ish (roughness
; 0.85, metallic 0), no texture and no emission: nothing in this room may glow except a product,
; and nothing structural should compete with the one object the seeker is hunting.
;
; THIS PREFAB IS LEVEL GEOMETRY, SO IT IS LISTED IN SupermarketWorldSelfTest.SectionScenes. It
; carries no script and builds nothing, which is exactly why the listing is cheap — but the list
; is the only mechanism that notices a prefab at all (godot-scenes.md, CLOCK-1), so being
; obviously safe today is not a reason to be absent from it.

